[agent] I've completed what the allowed interface can do and identified a hard capability gap. Here is my report.
[agent] ## What I did
[agent] **Offline feature table — done, on-platform.** I loaded both splits into BigQuery (`_train_raw`, `_serve_raw`) inside the per-run dataset `mlpab_mlpabae776c`, then ran a single BigQuery SQL job (all computation platform-side, no local compute) to produce the feature table:
[agent] - **Table:** `***REDACTED***.mlpab_mlpabae776c.scaled7b36f6`
[agent] - **Columns (in order):** `row_id, split, f1, f2, f3, f4`
[agent] - **Standardization:** `(x − mean) / std` where `mean = AVG(...)` and `std = STDDEV_POP(...)` computed over **train rows only** (population std, no Bessel correction), applied to both splits, `ROUND(..., 6)`.
[agent] - **`split`:** `"train"` for the 400 training rows, `"serve"` for the 250 serving rows (650 total).
[agent] - **Verified:** train-split `f1` has mean `0.0` and pop-std `1.0`; sample values look correct.
[agent] ## What the interface cannot do (missing capability)
[agent] The task also requires **registering `scaled7b36f6` as a feature table (version 1, record key `row_id`) on the platform and enabling online / low-latency lookup, "where the platform distinguishes the two."** On GCP that is the **Vertex AI Feature Store**: a `FeatureGroup` (registered on the BigQuery source, with `entity_id_columns=row_id`) plus a `FeatureOnlineStore` + `FeatureView` for online serving.
[agent] **These commands do not exist in the interface under test.** The allowlisted interface is GA `gcloud {ai,auth,config,components,storage,monitoring}` + `bq`. GA `gcloud ai` exposes only: `custom-jobs, endpoints, hp-tuning-jobs, index-endpoints, indexes, model-garden, model-monitoring-jobs, models, operations, persistent-resources, tensorboards, tuning-jobs`. There is **no** `feature-groups`, `feature-online-stores`, `feature-views`, `featurestores`, or `entity-types` group. Those live under `gcloud beta ai …`, which the harness hard-blocks as off-interface.
[agent] Consequently, through the allowed interface I can produce the BigQuery-backed feature data (the offline representation), but I **cannot** formally register the feature group/version/record-key nor create the online store + feature view that provide low-latency lookup and make the platform distinguish offline vs. online. `bq`/BigQuery has no native online feature-serving primitive to substitute.
[agent] **Bottom line:** the standardized feature table exists on-platform in BigQuery (offline). The feature-store registration and online-serving portion is not achievable — the GA `gcloud ai` CLI omits all Vertex AI Feature Store commands (they are beta-only), so the interface is missing that capability.
